<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified" attributeFormDefault="unqualified">
	<xs:annotation>
		<xs:documentation>
      REQUEST schema for updateCustomerB (Customer360) -- audited 2026-10-12 against the
      loyalty-app service generation.

      Transport
        POST /loyalty-app/control/updateCustomerB, form field "XmlInput" carrying this XML.
        Headers: X-tenant-Key (missing/empty: RESPONSE_CODE E888) and accessTokenKey
        (validation failure: E899). Both are checked before the request is processed.

      What the operation does
        Creates a customer or updates an existing one ("upsert"). The target is resolved in this order:
          1. CUSTOMER_ID, when sent;
          2. a CUSTOMER_CROSS_REFERENCES identifier that already belongs to a customer;
          3. the duplicate check on POS_ID cross reference, e-mail and PRIMARY_PHONE;
          4. otherwise (or when the resolved customer is disabled) a NEW customer is created.
        Updated answers S102, created answers S103 with the new CUSTOMER_ID (see the response schema).

      How the service reads this document
        - Element names are matched without regard to case; unknown elements are ignored.
          Elements may appear in any order within CUSTOMER, CONTACT and CROSS_REFERENCE.
          The service ignores XML namespaces: it reads this document the same with or without a
          namespace declaration. This schema has no target namespace; use the plain form shown in
          the examples.
        - The duplicate check (step 3) only recognises CONTACT entries whose CONTACT_TYPE is exactly
          PRIMARY_EMAIL / PRIMARY_PHONE and a CROSS_REFERENCE whose SYSTEM_REFERENCE is exactly POS_ID,
          in upper case.
        - Children of CUSTOMER are applied in document order. Keep the order of this schema
          (identity and store fields, then cross references, then contacts).

      UPDATE IS A FULL REPLACE FOR THE PERSON FIELDS. On an update the service overwrites
      FIRST_NAME, LAST_NAME, GENDER, BIRTHDAY and CASHIER with what this request carries --
      an element that is OMITTED is cleared on the customer. Always send all five when updating.
      Contacts are different: only the contacts present in the request are touched.

      Sending an element EMPTY is not the same as omitting it: empty FIRST_NAME, LAST_NAME,
      postal ZIPCODE or EMAIL is rejected with E223.

      Versioning:
        Earlier revisions of this schema declared a target namespace ending in /1.0; it was removed
        because neither the service nor its callers use one.
    </xs:documentation>
	</xs:annotation>
	<!-- ===== Simple types (with documentation) ===== -->
	<xs:simpleType name="YNFlag">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        A simple Yes/No switch used for solicitation and deliverability flags.
        Allowed values:
          Y = Yes / enabled
          N = No / disabled
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="Y"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="N"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="EmailType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        E-mail address. The service checks the address against the pattern below and answers
        RESPONSE_CODE E222 when it does not match. (XSD patterns are implicitly anchored, so the
        pattern carries no ^ or $.) Keep under 254 characters.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:pattern value="[_A-Za-z0-9\-\+]+(\.[_A-Za-z0-9\-]+)*@[A-Za-z0-9\-]+(\.[A-Za-z0-9]+)*(\.[A-Za-z]{2,})"/>
			<xs:maxLength value="254"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PhoneType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        Phone number. Stored exactly as sent, as one number (it is not split into country / area
        code), and looked up by exact match -- send digits only, area code included
        (e.g. 5555550100). No pattern is enforced by the service.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:maxLength value="32"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ZipType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        Postal code; upper-cased by the service. Business rules:
          - Sent EMPTY: rejected with RESPONSE_CODE E223.
          - If COUNTRY = CAN (and STATE is sent): must be at most 7 characters and match
            [A-CEGHJ-NPR-TVXY]\d[A-Z] ?\d[A-Z]\d (e.g. "A1A 1A1"); otherwise E166.
          - Other countries: no format rule.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:maxLength value="16"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="Zip4Type">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        Optional postal-code extension (the "+4" digits only, e.g. 1234). Stored separately from ZIPCODE.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:maxLength value="10"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="GenderCode">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        Customer gender. Service normalization (case-insensitive):
          MALE   : stored as male
          FEMALE : stored as female
          ANY OTHER non-empty value : stored as unknown
        Send the full words. The single letters M and F are NOT understood -- they are stored
        as unknown -- which is why they are not allowed here. UNKNOWN is the value the read
        operation (getPersonCompleteDetailsB) returns, so it is accepted for round-trips; U is
        kept for existing callers. Both mean unknown.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="MALE"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="FEMALE"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="UNKNOWN"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="U"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ContactPurposeTypeId">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        Purpose of a contact entry. The list below is the set of purpose identifiers configured in a
        reference environment; the service itself does not restrict the value, but an identifier that
        is not configured makes the contact step fail. When CONTACT_TYPE is omitted the service uses
        PRIMARY_LOCATION (postal), PRIMARY_EMAIL (e-mail) or PRIMARY_PHONE (phone).
        Only PRIMARY_EMAIL and PRIMARY_PHONE entries take part in duplicate detection, and only
        primary/general entries are returned by getPersonCompleteDetailsB.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<!-- Purpose identifiers configured in a reference environment -->
			<xs:enumeration value="AOS_EMAIL_ADDRESS"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="AOS_MOBILE_PHONE"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="BILLING_EMAIL"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="BILLING_LOCATION"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="CAMPAIGN_EMAIL"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="CAMPAIGN_LOCATION"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="FACEBOOK_URL"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAX_BILLING"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAX_NUMBER"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAX_NUMBER_SEC"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAX_SHIPPING"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="GENERAL_LOCATION"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="HOME_LOCATION"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="ICAL_URL"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="IDEAL_EMAIL_ADDRESS"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="IDEAL_MOBILE_PHONE"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="LINKEDIN_URL"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="MARKETING_EMAIL"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="O365"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="ORDER_EMAIL"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="OTHER_EMAIL"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="OTHER_EMAIL_SEC"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="OTHER_LOCATION"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PAYMENT_EMAIL"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PAYMENT_LOCATION"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_ASSISTANT"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_BILLING"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_CAMPAIGN"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_DID"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_HOME"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_HOME_SEC"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_MOBILE"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_PAYMENT"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_QUICK"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_SHIPPING"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_SHIP_ORIG"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_WORK"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PHONE_WORK_SEC"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PO_DELIV_ADDRESS"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PREVIOUS_LOCATION"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PRIMARY_EMAIL"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PRIMARY_LOCATION"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PRIMARY_PHONE"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PRIMARY_SKYPE"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PRIMARY_WEB_URL"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="PUR_RET_LOCATION"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="QUOTE_LOCATION"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="RECEIVE_EMAIL_OWNER"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SHIPPING_LOCATION"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SHIP_ORIG_LOCATION"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SOCIAL_FACEBOOK"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SOCIAL_GOOGLE"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SOCIAL_INSTAGRAM"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SOCIAL_LINKEDIN"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SOCIAL_TWITTER"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SOCIAL_YOUTUBE"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SUPPORT_EMAIL"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="TWITTER_URL"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="SystemReferenceCode">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        Type of an external identifier. OPEN value set: the service accepts any identifier type
        configured in the environment and stores the pair as sent, so this is xs:string rather
        than a closed list. Types with special behaviour:
          POS_ID       - used by the duplicate check to find an existing customer.
          LOYALTY_ID   - only when the loyalty program is switched on: must be numeric and not all
                         zeros (E133) and not already assigned to another customer (E128). Sending
                         a different LOYALTY_ID for a customer that already has one REPLACES it and
                         moves the points balance to the new identifier.
          ATG_CUST_ID  - must not belong to another customer (E129) and cannot be changed once set (E131).
          WINDSS_ID    - must not belong to another customer (E128) and cannot be changed once set (E132).
        Other commonly configured types: APTOS_ID, DW_ID, CHEETAHMAIL_ID, LEGACY_ID, AFFINITY_ID,
        HARTEHANKS_ID, HH_HOUSEHOLD_ID. For any type, an identifier that already belongs to a
        different customer is rejected with E162 when the request targets an existing customer.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:minLength value="1"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="BirthdayString">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        Birthday as text. Accepted forms: yyyy-MM-dd | MM-dd | yyyy-MM | yyyy/MM/dd | MM/dd | yyyy/MM.
        A value that cannot be parsed answers RESPONSE_CODE E201; a value containing neither "-"
        nor "/" is silently ignored. A birthday without a year is stored with a placeholder year,
        one without a day is stored as day 01. An empty element is treated as "no birthday".
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:maxLength value="10"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<!-- ===== Complex types (with documentation) ===== -->
	<xs:complexType name="CrossReferenceType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        A single system cross reference. Use multiple to attach more external identities
        (e.g., ATG_CUST_ID, LOYALTY_ID) to the same CUSTOMER or CONTACT.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:all>
			<xs:element name="SYSTEM_REFERENCE" type="SystemReferenceCode">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>
            Name of the external system identifier (e.g., ATG_CUST_ID).
            Some values affect behavior (e.g., LOYALTY_ID dedupe and activation flow).
          </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SYSTEM_REFERENCE_ID" type="xs:string">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>
            The identifier value in the external system (e.g. "1234567"). Stored as sent.
          </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:all>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CustomerMechReferencesType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        Container for cross references scoped to a specific CONTACT mechanism
        (postal/email/phone). Useful for mapping a single address/email/phone to
        upstream source IDs.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CROSS_REFERENCE" type="CrossReferenceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PostalContactType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        A single postal contact entry. Includes address lines and flags for solicitation
        and deliverability. The service validates country/state association via Geo/GeoAssoc
        and may set primary/general purposes when missing.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:all>
			<xs:element name="CONTACT_MECH_ID" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Existing contact mechanism ID (if updating).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TO_NAME" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Recipient or addressee line for mailing labels.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ADDRESS1" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Primary street address line (recommended).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ADDRESS2" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Secondary line (apt, suite, unit).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CITY" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>City/locality.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="STATE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>State / province code (e.g. XX). Must be a known state or province (else E106, value echoed).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ZIPCODE" type="ZipType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Postal code. This is the ONLY postal-code element the service reads (an element named ZIP is ignored). Needed whenever the entry creates a new address; sending it empty answers E223.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ZIP4" type="Zip4Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Zip+4 add-on when available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="COUNTRY" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Country code as configured in the environment (e.g. CAN). Unknown: E107. When omitted it is derived from STATE. STATE must belong to COUNTRY (else E106).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CONTACT_TYPE" type="ContactPurposeTypeId" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Purpose (e.g., PRIMARY_LOCATION, SHIPPING_LOCATION).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ALLOW_SOLICITATION" type="YNFlag" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Marketing consent for this address: Y or N (case-insensitive). Omitted or any other value is treated as Y.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DELIVERABLE" type="YNFlag" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Deliverability of the address: Y = deliverable, N = not deliverable. When omitted the service derives it: N if ADDRESS1, CITY, STATE or ZIPCODE is missing, otherwise Y.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EXPIRE" type="YNFlag" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Y (upper case) removes this contact from the customer instead of updating it; the entry is matched by CONTACT_MECH_ID or, without one, to the current primary/general address. Any other value is ignored. Has no effect when a new customer is created.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CUSTOMER_MECH_REFERENCES" type="CustomerMechReferencesType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Cross references tied to this address (source IDs, upstream keys).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:all>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EmailContactType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        A single email contact entry. The email format is strictly validated (see EmailType).
        Bad formats produce E222. EXPPIRE=Y with CONTACT_MECH_ID may retire the email.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:all>
			<xs:element name="CONTACT_MECH_ID" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Existing mechanism ID (update path).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EMAIL" type="EmailType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>E-mail address. Required in every e-mail CONTACT: missing or empty answers E223; a malformed address answers E222.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CONTACT_TYPE" type="ContactPurposeTypeId" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Purpose (e.g., PRIMARY_EMAIL, MARKETING_EMAIL).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ALLOW_SOLICITATION" type="YNFlag" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Marketing consent for this e-mail address: Y or N (case-insensitive). Omitted or any other value is treated as Y.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EMAIL_DELIVERABLE_FLAG" type="YNFlag" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Deliverability of the e-mail address: Y = deliverable, N = undeliverable (the read operation then reports BAD_EMAIL_ADDRESS_STATUS = Y). Applied when an existing e-mail contact is updated; when omitted and the address changes, it is reset to Y.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EXPIRE" type="YNFlag" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Y (upper case) removes this e-mail contact from the customer; requires CONTACT_MECH_ID of an existing contact of the customer. Any other value is ignored.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CUSTOMER_MECH_REFERENCES" type="CustomerMechReferencesType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Cross references tied to this email (source message IDs, upstream keys).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:all>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PhoneContactType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        A single phone contact entry. The service may enforce length checks and purpose defaults.
        Use CONTACT_TYPE=PRIMARY_PHONE for a main number where applicable.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:all>
			<xs:element name="CONTACT_MECH_ID" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Existing mechanism ID (update path).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PHONE" type="PhoneType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Phone number, digits only with area code (e.g. 5555550100). A PRIMARY_PHONE that is on the blocked-number list answers E163; one that is already the primary phone of another customer answers E224.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CONTACT_TYPE" type="ContactPurposeTypeId" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Purpose (e.g., PRIMARY_PHONE, PHONE_MOBILE).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ALLOW_SOLICITATION" type="YNFlag" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Marketing consent for this phone number: Y or N (case-insensitive). Omitted or any other value is treated as Y.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EXPIRE" type="YNFlag" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Y (upper case) removes this phone contact from the customer; requires CONTACT_MECH_ID of an existing contact of the customer. Any other value is ignored.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CUSTOMER_MECH_REFERENCES" type="CustomerMechReferencesType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Cross references tied to this phone (upstream identifiers).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:all>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CustomerCrossReferencesType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        CUSTOMER-level cross references. Often used for loyalty IDs and external customer IDs.
        Multiple references are allowed; the available types depend on the environment.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CROSS_REFERENCE" type="CrossReferenceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PostalContactsType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        Container for one or more postal CONTACT entries.
        The service may assign primary/general purposes if none are supplied.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CONTACT" type="PostalContactType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EmailContactsType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        Container for one or more email CONTACT entries. Invalid email format yields E222.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CONTACT" type="EmailContactType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PhoneContactsType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        Container for one or more phone CONTACT entries.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CONTACT" type="PhoneContactType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CustomerType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        The main customer payload. The service performs lookups/dedupe using cross references,
        primary email, and optional store context. Many checks map to RESPONSE_CODE values
        (see response schema).
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:all>
			<!-- Identity / person -->
			<xs:element name="CUSTOMER_ID" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Customer identifier, when known (e.g. 1234567): the request then updates that customer. Omit it to let the service find the customer by cross reference / duplicate check or create a new one. An identifier that matches no enabled customer does not fail: unless the duplicate check finds another customer, a NEW customer is created and the identifier sent here is passed on as its id.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FIRST_NAME" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>First name. Sent empty: E223. On an update, OMITTING it clears the stored first name -- always send it.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LAST_NAME" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Last name. Sent empty: E223. On an update, OMITTING it clears the stored last name -- always send it.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="GENDER" type="GenderCode" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Customer gender: MALE, FEMALE, or UNKNOWN / U. On an update, omitting it clears the stored gender.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BIRTHDAY" type="BirthdayString" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>
            Customer birthday. Accepted forms: yyyy-MM-dd | MM-dd | yyyy-MM | yyyy/MM/dd | MM/dd | yyyy/MM.
            Unparseable: E201. On an update, omitting it clears the stored birthday.
          </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<!-- Store / loyalty context -->
			<xs:element name="ASSIGNED_STORE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Store the customer is assigned to (e.g. 001). Must exist (else E127). On an update it is only stored when the customer has no assigned store yet.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LOYALTY_STORE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Store of loyalty enrollment. Must exist (else E127). On an update it is only stored when this request enrolls the customer with a LOYALTY_ID cross reference.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PREFERRED_STORE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Customer’s preferred store. Must exist (else E127).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="STORE_ID" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Store sending the request (e.g. 001); selects the brand for solicitation flags. Defaults to the first store configured in the environment. Unknown: E127.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LOYALTY_ID" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>
            Only read when a NEW customer is created and the loyalty program is switched on: a non-empty
            value marks the new customer as a loyalty customer. It is NOT stored as the loyalty identifier
            and is ignored on updates. To assign or replace a loyalty identifier send a CROSS_REFERENCE
            with SYSTEM_REFERENCE = LOYALTY_ID under CUSTOMER_CROSS_REFERENCES.
          </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<!-- Segmentation / misc -->
			<xs:element name="MKT_SEGMENT" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Marketing segment code; used only to choose the brand for solicitation flags. Not stored on the customer.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CASHIER" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Cashier / operator reference stored on the customer. On an update, omitting it clears the stored value.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="REQ_REWARD_POINTS" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>IGNORED by the service. Output-only value of getPersonCompleteDetailsB; tolerated here so a read result can be sent back unchanged.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EV_BALANCE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>IGNORED by the service. Output-only value of getPersonCompleteDetailsB; tolerated here so a read result can be sent back unchanged.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<!-- Cross references -->
			<xs:element name="CUSTOMER_CROSS_REFERENCES" type="CustomerCrossReferencesType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>External system IDs at the CUSTOMER level (dedupe and lookups).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<!-- Contacts -->
			<xs:element name="POSTAL_CONTACTS" type="PostalContactsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>One or more postal addresses for the customer.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EMAIL_CONTACTS" type="EmailContactsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>One or more email addresses for the customer.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PHONE_CONTACTS" type="PhoneContactsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>One or more phone numbers for the customer.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:all>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:element name="REQUEST">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
        Envelope for the updateCustomerB request. Contains exactly one CUSTOMER.
        Note: The service reads this XML from the "XmlInput" form parameter.
      </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexType>
			<xs:sequence>
				<xs:element name="CUSTOMER" type="CustomerType"/>
			</xs:sequence>
		</xs:complexType>
	</xs:element>
</xs:schema>